import json
p='country_unique.json'
raw=open(p,encoding='utf8',newline='').read()
d=json.loads(raw)
H={
'croatia':"Croatia's customs pages split tobacco by transport: 200 cigarettes arriving by air or sea from a third country, 40 by road or rail, plus 10 ml of e-liquid and 50 g of heated tobacco. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more is declared on form HR1 or EN1. Seeds and plants for planting must be shown at one of seven border inspection posts, including Zagreb airport and the ports of Ploče and Rijeka.",
'france':"French customs lets you split the tobacco and alcohol allowances proportionally, so using half of one leaves half of another. Under-17s get no duty-free tobacco or alcohol. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more is declared online through the DALIA service, up to 30 days before the trip. A phytosanitary certificate is needed from the first plant specimen, and soil, grapevines and citrus plants are prohibited.",
'ireland':"Irish Revenue lets you split the spirits and weaker-drink allowances, for example 0.5 litre of spirits with 1 litre of port, and the tobacco allowance fractionally. Oral smokeless tobacco is generally prohibited. Customs can seize cash of EUR 1,000 or more it suspects is linked to crime, apart from the EUR 10,000 declaration. Plants are checked by the Department of Agriculture at Dublin Port, Dublin Airport and Rosslare Europort.",
'italy':"Italy's customs agency counts each allowance as 100%, so any mix of tobacco or alcohol is fine if the shares add up to no more than 100%. Goods above the allowance can be left in customs custody for 90 days while formalities are completed. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more is declared at a customs office. Plant foods for personal use that need no certificate are capped at 5 kg fresh or 2 kg dried.",
'poland':"Poland's duty-free exemption for tobacco and alcohol starts at age 17, not 18. Border-zone residents and workers and vehicle crews have their own, lower limits. Between Schengen countries cash need not be declared, but crossing the Schengen border with EUR 10,000 or more must be. For plants, Poland's inspectorate separates plants not for planting, which may enter at any crossing, from seeds and planting material, which need a designated inspection post and a TRACES NT notification.",
'portugal':"Portugal's tax authority guide of February 2026 allows 200 cigarettes, 1 litre of spirits or 2 litres of intermediate products such as fortified wine, and gives separate allowances for heated tobacco, e-liquid and nicotine pouches. Travellers under 17 get no tobacco or alcohol allowance. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more, including gold since June 2021, is declared through the customs portal. The food and veterinary authority warns that plants for planting carry a high pest risk.",
'slovakia':"The Slovak Financial Administration allows 200 cigarettes plus ten packs of smokeless tobacco by air, but 40 cigarettes plus two packs by other transport, from age 17. Alcohol includes 2 litres of sparkling wine alongside 4 litres of still wine and 16 litres of beer. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more must be reported in writing to the border customs office, on form 1a for accompanied cash. Plants may be carried in small amounts only for use during the journey and without pest risk.",
'slovenia':"Slovenia's tax administration (FURS) grants the tobacco and alcohol relief only for goods carried occasionally for personal or family use or as presents, never to under-17s. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more is declared on the official form at the EU external border. The food safety administration counts fruit, vegetables, potted plants, substrates, sowing material and cut flowers as plants, and most need a certificate and inspection on prior notification.",
'spain':"Spain's tax agency cuts tobacco to 80 cigarettes for residents and workers within 15 km of the Gibraltar border, and cuts allowances to one tenth for international transport staff. Cash of EUR 10,000 or more per person and trip is declared on form E1 or E2 for non-EU trips; movements within Spain are declared from EUR 100,000. Live plants must be declared whatever the quantity and must be free of soil, and potatoes and tubers must always be declared.",
}
for c,t in H.items():
    d['hub'][c]['p'].append(t)
open(p,'w',encoding='utf8',newline='').write(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))+('\n' if raw.endswith('\n') else ''))
